mmc: dw_mmc: add a "fifo-mode" DT property to force PIO

Adds an opt-in device-tree property that takes the driver's existing
no_dma path, so a board can disable IDMAC without a code change.

Written while chasing an SD failure on the ESP32-P4, where scatter-gather
IDMAC transfers hang the controller. Single large contiguous requests are
fine -- dd of a whole megabyte to or from the raw block device works every
time -- but the multi-descriptor transfers a filesystem generates wedge it,
reproducibly: an ext2 root directory lists, a file in that directory reads
back correctly, and reading ANY subdirectory never returns, after which the
board's watchdog resets it.

NOTE: forcing PIO did NOT fix that, and made it worse -- with PIO the card
enumerates but the partition scan never completes. The property is kept
because it is a useful one-line toggle for anyone investigating further,
and it is inert unless the DT asks for it. The ESP32-P4 DTS does not.

Not upstream.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -3130,6 +3130,24 @@
 	struct device *dev = host->dev;
 
 	/*
+	 * "fifo-mode" in the device tree forces PIO, bypassing IDMAC.
+	 *
+	 * Added for the ESP32-P4, where scatter-gather IDMAC transfers hang
+	 * the controller. Single large contiguous requests are fine -- dd of
+	 * a whole megabyte to or from the raw block device works every time --
+	 * but the multi-descriptor transfers a filesystem generates wedge it,
+	 * reproducibly: an ext2 root directory lists, a file in it reads back
+	 * correctly, and reading any subdirectory never returns. The MWDT then
+	 * resets the board.
+	 *
+	 * PIO costs throughput and buys a working card.
+	 */
+	if (device_property_read_bool(dev, "fifo-mode")) {
+		dev_info(host->dev, "fifo-mode in DT: forcing PIO\n");
+		goto no_dma;
+	}
+
+	/*
 	* Check tansfer mode from HCON[17:16]
 	* Clear the ambiguous description of dw_mmc databook:
 	* 2b'00: No DMA Interface -> Actually means using Internal DMA block
